    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d387">

                <pb facs="0512" n="427" xml:id="pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3052: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-14T12:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 14, 1919,
                                noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 15,
                            9.22 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>I had an informal conversation with the Minister for Foreign Affairs this
                    afternoon. I took occasion to refer to the Tientsin agitations [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">affair</hi>] in the tenor of your April 11th, 7 p.m. He
                    advised me that he has telegraphed to Obata<anchor n="30" xml:id="d387-f1"/>
                    summary of facts, left with Vice-Minister for Foreign Affairs last week and has
                    instructed Obata to make the necessary amends if it appeared from his
                    investigation that any of the Japanese involved were at fault.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d387-f1" n="30" xml:id="d387-f1-content">
                <p>Torikichi Obata, Japanese Minister to China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
